   "raw_files_location": "raw-feeds/ beside this file, kept out of git. NVD overwrites its feeds daily, so this is the only copy of the snapshot the numbers rest on."
  },
  "scanner_table": "src/phantomprobe/cpe_tables.py at commit 18175f55f8 (release 0.9.3): 74 products, 25 second identifiers",
  "method": [
   "1_dict_aggregate.py reduces the dictionary to one row per part:vendor:product and to a rename map: an edge from identifier A to identifier B wherever a CPE name under A is deprecated in favour of a name under B.",
   "2_cve_index.py reads every CVE that is not rejected and records the identifiers of its match criteria marked vulnerable. A CVE is 'filed under' an identifier when it appears there.",
   "4_measure.py and 5_refine.py compare, for every pair of application identifiers a rename links, the CVEs filed under each. A rename is 'complete' when every name under the old identifier is deprecated and all point at one new identifier.",
   "3_table_candidates.py proposes, for each product in the scanner's table, other identifiers by three rules: a rename link (any number of hops), the same product name under another vendor, and a related product name under the same vendor.",
   "data/classification.json records which proposals were judged the same software. 6_table_recall.py then compares three sets per product: the table's identifier alone, the identifiers 0.9.3 queries, and the complete same-software set."
  ],
  "caveats": [
   "All counts are version-independent: they say an identifier holds a CVE, not that any particular version is affected.",
   "81617 of the 406711 CVEs kept have no identifier at all yet. No identifier-based lookup can find them, and they are outside every figure here.",
   "A rename edge is drawn from name-level deprecations. 236 of the 1,903 application pairs are partial (some names moved, not the product), so the headline figures use the 1,667 complete renames.",
   "Whether a proposed identifier is the same software is a single-rater judgement made by the AI assistant that ran the study. A paper needs a second rater.",
   "The three rules miss real cases: 4 of the 25 second identifiers the scanner already queries are found by none of them. The complete set is therefore a lower bound on what a single identifier misses.",
   "Only application identifiers were analysed for renames, not hardware or operating systems.",
   "The table-level figures describe one scanner's 74 products. The dictionary-wide figures do not depend on it."
  ],
  "files": {
   "data/identifiers.tsv.gz": "every identifier in the dictionary with its name counts",
   "data/rename_edges.json": "the rename map",
   "data/cve_identifiers.tsv.gz": "every kept CVE with its identifiers",
   "data/cve_feed_checks.json": "size and sha256 of each yearly CVE file against NVD",
   "data/measure.json": "per-pair and per-candidate counts",
   "data/refine.json": "complete and partial renames, timeline, titles",
   "data/table_candidates.json": "what each rule proposed for each product",
   "data/classification.json": "the same-software judgements and their reasons",
   "data/table_recall.json": "per-product completeness",
   "scripts/": "the six scripts in the order they were run"
  }
 },
